bound-lock/1 about="what topos is, in its own words, at the epoch this line was signed: bound's SDK, the wire, the forms, the contract and the shell a world is built with, a reader of any source or a renderer of any artefact; and that it knows no world, produces no text and writes no order of its own" at=witness:an-sdk-whose-what-still-said-notation by=target form=alphabet measure=status needs=docs/what.md restsOn=sha256:b8d64006eed800e8341a70f6a216cd94f6ba47c5873411a792bc6bc1f26aeef1 role=demands scope=docs/what shape=render value=present
bound-lock/1 about="{\"contract\":\"Captured diagnostics are a declared projection, not a raw transcript: only the absolute reader location within stderr is replaced by <place>/<reader basename>. Every status, stdout, refusal cause, case, module commitment and remaining diagnostic character stays unchanged. Originals remain private and are identified by digest. This projection never changes receipt payload identity or claims to rerun a case.\",\"files\":[{\"file\":\"vectors/native/adoption.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:67cf6d54b23d78a5c4447902fde9bd773485eff7e078f1d2d2667656d92fd7f4\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:453d0ac4122062e27b5191b61171b0df05b7316f207dd1bcf1754708c0111e82\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/authority-eligibility.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:b9e5aedc7a867e8fcd51eae42d3b4cacd076f5fb1cdeffb74d34b4ef492a784b\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:5a7609f73573471e8f9a3994392c2a0920469d611747e234a308436c1f683103\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/command-port.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:db465f7a4c4435fc6f7eaa5eefd80a553c801c767ef09e3c036147177ad4a090\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:301a2500cd2afcad1e4cff94808c9df8b6b8c43db3cc0407309a103a280ada06\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/inspection-lineage.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:30e76ebb37e82e1193244a1c806d436aed0e3aa64044c01620bde5d7d8d42b9a\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:9b082eac433917cf63924beea3b367c3801b72654715e6c9bd955ac492f4e977\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/origins-snapshots.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:8b6afc490112f7614c933037fd14134cd2aa5eb2a181047fdba9dc2efad912de\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:681cdb3b7af81eaea04f259575a1bcf1b88aa474c62725d61dfcfdb00218fa75\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/place-act-context.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:db5579f811cf52863d6da01b2601d11f30f41927f376b40ba88e3b50e1bbab91\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:d8925621a18d8e7d8d314b5f24ce64799f470e6ebd9b1b7dffe0717f236f8930\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/place-inputs.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:16e615f00d4434664278b9ef8fef951a8f976452d19c07b45d9a3fe3672cbfb0\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:12ce7142552af226c9b42d385e909b87ce7858254670f70dc33e6869e2e1c224\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/policy.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:e76138e67bbfc105122736738d90c608c57fdc76ba149dfd091eb273e05a729e\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:b4a6d84fd8c07523f5ac4f9962fc9ab88a7c590e8b89cb537245edf9e68f575c\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/reading-identity.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:e58e0be4a055d41d314c6eda095f44ffc9f0f42d5f4271988b8e937c068d7ca8\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:e035b8ba35afd8506c578d630daf86aa3835c0d84b31582008307f289bf2fdf4\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/readings.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:b6fc5f7ba82d179767cbfcaf3f553a89530af7cd70d8de3d5b2a7b11a3b3001b\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:98c6c9a2c44cdcff55f0f1b1f5c597bf182402fbefd81d2a7c9bf074505c82e3\"},{\"file\":\"vectors/native/shadow.cli.json\",\"oldDigest\":\"sha256:9f535481928a3e422250a6527f4ab9d6c4e498174c3aa246d4ebe876d73dafed\",\"newDigest\":\"sha256:5b619365bbba0816d2344f523437b5fd377f06577bf4fa1566e02ecc64dc5feb\"}]}" at=witness:public-native-diagnostics by=target form=alphabet measure=id needs=vectors/native/adoption.cli.json|vectors/native/authority-eligibility.cli.json|vectors/native/command-port.cli.json|vectors/native/inspection-lineage.cli.json|vectors/native/origins-snapshots.cli.json|vectors/native/place-act-context.cli.json|vectors/native/place-inputs.cli.json|vectors/native/policy.cli.json|vectors/native/reading-identity.cli.json|vectors/native/readings.cli.json|vectors/native/shadow.cli.json role=writes scope=audit/native-capture-diagnostics value=projected-reader-location@1
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"bound-lock/1-compatibility\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Reuse existing lexical and epoch-sensitive wire expectations; no wire or algebra change.\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Meaning is independent of a particular owner selection or release.\",\n  \"contract\": [\n    \"Golden lexical cases, UTF-8 distinction and effective-epoch field cases use the existing parser, canonicalizer and wireAt/fromLine implementation.\",\n    \"No new field, grammar or old-profile extension is introduced by the new contract profiles.\",\n    \"An altered expected canonical byte string refuses rather than accepting a new baseline.\",\n    \"Retirement/publication mechanics are retained evidence, not a newly invented inverse or syntax.\"\n  ],\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"A producer not represented by these fixtures must provide its own exact compatibility vector\"\n  ],\n  \"quartet\": {\n    \"contract\": \"docs/contracts/wire-compatibility.json\",\n    \"positive\": \"samples/wire-compatibility/yes/*.json\",\n    \"vector\": \"vectors/native/wire-compatibility.cli.json\",\n    \"negative\": \"samples/wire-compatibility/no/*.json\"\n  },\n  \"readerBudgetMs\": 5000\n}\n" at=witness:reference-wire-catalog-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/wire-compatibility-data shape=docs/contracts/wire-compatibility.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-action-link-contract/1\",\n  \"profiles\": [\n    \"topos-action-receipt/1\",\n    \"topos-authenticated-link/1\"\n  ],\n  \"purpose\": \"Bind action context and reference identity to an existing native act receipt\",\n  \"reuses\": [\n    \"actResultOf\",\n    \"actIdentity\",\n    \"decodeLocatedReference\",\n    \"locatedReferenceIdentity\",\n    \"inspectLocatedReference\"\n  ],\n  \"interpretation\": \"One admitted signed record at the consumer-selected statement scope commits SHA256 of the canonical action statement plus LF. The native act receipt covers that record through the existing native verification contract. The packet names the native act identity and SHA256 of the receipt plus LF. No record is signed, admitted, persisted or committed by this API.\",\n  \"statement\": [\n    \"verb\",\n    \"request/result digests\",\n    \"key/place/region\",\n    \"before/policy/catalog/standingContract digests\"\n  ],\n  \"link\": \"Emitter and region bind to the action. Result commits SHA256 of locatedReferenceIdentity plus LF. Location is excluded from that existing identity and remains unauthenticated; a replacement locator cannot replace content identity. Missing bytes remain needs/bytes/<blob>; corrupt bytes refuse integrity, never fork. Object-history authentication is separate.\",\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Receiver selects native scope/context and expected statement; packets cannot choose trust keys or verifiers\",\n    \"Native consumer guarantees durable commit, recovery and no duplicate effect; parser repetition does not prove those properties\"\n  ],\n  \"nativeScope\": \"Two receiver fixtures use public native act verification and the existing authority-at-epoch relation with disposable signature adapters. No production storage transaction is claimed.\",\n  \"resourceContract\": \"Caller supplies byte and per-collection item budgets; no ambient clock, I/O, default verifier or universal region list\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Contract meaning only. Admission, production consumer verification and public delivery require their separate acta.\"\n}\n" at=witness:authority-and-governance-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/action-link-data shape=docs/contracts/action-link.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-algebra-consumption/1\",\n  \"scope\": \"Focused consumed-surface comparison, not equivalence of all theorems or native admission\",\n  \"input\": \"Selected public Obligations package, prepared manifest/lock, actual consumed source and captured cross-version outputs\",\n  \"witness\": \"Equal snapshot digests and successful focused runs; not a statement that distinct implementations inherit receipts\",\n  \"implementationBoundary\": \"Reuse existing Topos/Obligations operations; the reader checks the sealed evidence and selected dependency identity, without another algebra or authority judge\",\n  \"publishedMetadataDebt\": \"Obligations0.4.7 region-measure/key-lineage contracts retain contradictory lifecycle labels; no correction or upgrade is implied\",\n  \"refusal\": [\n    \"missing or altered declared input\",\n    \"changed selected dependency\",\n    \"different compared snapshot\",\n    \"failed captured run\"\n  ],\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Selected standing, admission receipts and release approval establish lifecycle separately\"\n}\n" at=witness:contextual-reading-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/algebra-alignment-data shape=docs/contracts/algebra-alignment.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-authority-card/1\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Contextual view of a consumer-produced authority judgment\",\n  \"reuses\": [\n    \"normalizeRegistryHorizon\",\n    \"existing consumer authority evaluation\"\n  ],\n  \"commits\": [\n    \"place/snapshot\",\n    \"key/authority/coverage\",\n    \"policy/budget/demands\",\n    \"grants/retirements\",\n    \"catalog/standingContract\",\n    \"explicit horizon and issuedAt\",\n    \"request-digest decisions\",\n    \"external judgment evidence\"\n  ],\n  \"interpretation\": \"Parsing is a declaration, not permission. authorityCardAnswer compares current consumer context and explicit clock before accepting a judgment through a receiver-selected verification port. It never calculates allow/ask/deny from grants.\",\n  \"refusals\": [\n    \"card-stale\",\n    \"not-in-card\"\n  ],\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Verify the actual judge, signature/coverage, every statement/context binding and accepted clock source\",\n    \"Supply current authority identity after withdrawal, even when content snapshot is unchanged\"\n  ],\n  \"nativeScope\": \"Two receiver fixtures verify signature plus a fixed judgment statement. This is not a live production authority fold.\",\n  \"resourceContract\": \"Caller supplies byte and per-collection item budgets; no ambient clock, I/O, default verifier or universal region list\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Contract meaning only. Admission, production consumer verification and public delivery require their separate acta.\"\n}\n" at=witness:authority-and-governance-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/authority-card-data shape=docs/contracts/authority-card.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-governance-record/1\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Group, member and decision forms with declared k-of-n and prior-authority binding\",\n  \"reuses\": [\n    \"normalizeRegistryQuorum\",\n    \"normalizeRegistryHorizon\",\n    \"existing named-threshold@1 syntax\"\n  ],\n  \"interpretation\": \"Group names a set of regions and a snapshot. Member references a group by digest, named key, validity horizon and evidence. Decision references prior group, separate membership snapshot, exact proposal, context, threshold, horizon and proof references. Duplicate proof keys and impossible declared thresholds refuse structurally; proofs are not counted as verified votes.\",\n  \"identityBoundary\": \"The group does not contain hashes of members that hash the group again. Membership is a separately named snapshot. A next-group proposal excludes a backlink to its authorizing decision. The decision names prior-group and next-proposal digests.\",\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Native consumer resolves bytes, admitted member bindings, valid distinct signatures and eligibility at the declared deadline\",\n    \"Group change is authorized under the prior group, never the proposed group\",\n    \"Native consumer retains comparable admitted incompatible decisions as a named fork; opposed votes, corrupt bytes and distinct unverified declarations do not establish that fork\",\n    \"If native threshold admission is absent, keep governance/native-threshold-admission open\"\n  ],\n  \"nativeScope\": \"Two places demonstrate declared predecessor binding and reject self-authorization. Actual quorum execution, admission and independence remain not established.\",\n  \"resourceContract\": \"Caller supplies byte and per-collection item budgets; no ambient clock, I/O, default verifier or universal region list\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Contract meaning only. Admission, production consumer verification and public delivery require their separate acta.\"\n}\n" at=witness:authority-and-governance-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/group-decision-data shape=docs/contracts/group-decision.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-installed-acceptance/1\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Bind recorded installation, public API/types and native closure of an exact archive to the interpreted source/type identities.\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Interpretation is independent of selection or publication. This evidence names the archive actually installed, not a later changed delivery envelope.\",\n  \"contract\": [\n    \"The archive digest, size and member count identify the immutable pre-admission archive tested in two clean consumers.\",\n    \"Source/type/manifest/README/citation/public-lock identities are explicit; the current reading refuses any changed input.\",\n    \"Installation, API, type checking, README examples and native closure have separately captured outcomes and times.\",\n    \"Both consumers use verified published Obligations0.4.7; install scripts are disabled and no private store, ledger, CAS or source symlinks are copied.\",\n    \"121 public values and61 types from29 module bindings and18 subpaths are checked through installed exports, with12 relevant API cases.\",\n    \"42 native readings are retained with zero openings; their source histories are not relabeled as newly executed matrices.\",\n    \"Release-ready is refused: a changed post-admission archive requires exact member/installation verification before final approval.\",\n    \"These are committed observations, not proof of production authority, threshold admission, empirical calibration or physical-machine independence.\"\n  ],\n  \"quartet\": {\n    \"contract\": \"docs/contracts/installed-acceptance.json\",\n    \"positive\": \"vectors/native/installed-acceptance.cli.json#inputs[kind=yes]\",\n    \"vector\": \"vectors/native/installed-acceptance.cli.json#captures\",\n    \"negative\": \"vectors/native/installed-acceptance.cli.json#inputs[kind=no]\"\n  },\n  \"readerBudgetMs\": 5000,\n  \"pending\": [\n    \"Final archive after acceptance admission\",\n    \"Checkout/CI and public provider URLs\",\n    \"Existing external producer/authorization gaps\",\n    \"Unapproved stochastic model\",\n    \"Independent physical-machine portability\"\n  ]\n}\n" at=witness:installed-archive-acceptance by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/installed-acceptance-data shape=docs/contracts/installed-acceptance.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-origin-refusal-contract/1\",\n  \"profiles\": [\n    \"topos-attributed-origin/1\",\n    \"topos-written-refusal/1\"\n  ],\n  \"purpose\": \"Distinguish attributed source, authenticated covering proof and written refusal\",\n  \"reuses\": [\n    \"existing canonical wire\",\n    \"receiver-selected coverage verifier\"\n  ],\n  \"interpretation\": \"A named admitted key and unsigned origin line do not authenticate an author. A covering proof binds the canonical origin statement; its own evidence digest is excluded to avoid self-reference. Authenticated attribution is not authorization. A refusal names producer, code, request digest, scope, context and next action; decoding does not authenticate its producer.\",\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Actual key admission and signature/coverage under the selected context\",\n    \"Real key-material-request refusal is emitted by its consumer; Topos represents it and never owns the private signer\"\n  ],\n  \"nativeScope\": \"Two fixtures verify origin covering signatures with receiver-pinned public keys; sample refusal codes are attributed fixture declarations, not an admission or hijack verdict.\",\n  \"resourceContract\": \"Caller supplies byte and per-collection item budgets; no ambient clock, I/O, default verifier or universal region list\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Contract meaning only. Admission, production consumer verification and public delivery require their separate acta.\"\n}\n" at=witness:authority-and-governance-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/origin-refusal-data shape=docs/contracts/origin-refusal.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-physical-lines/1\",\n  \"domain\": \"Complete named-file snapshot and declared region selectors supplied by consumer; no implicit filesystem access\",\n  \"producer\": \"Topos readPhysicalLines with host-supplied digest primitive\",\n  \"model\": {\n    \"name\": \"finite-nonnegative-atomic-valuation@1\",\n    \"package\": \"@lapxo/obligations@0.4.7\",\n    \"contract\": \"sha256:636ace16eeaa46eafb7b07c28d1d57916bc9108b188e96b5a8bf7bed6dc15707\",\n    \"implementation\": \"sha256:ef7e39d0ac44b0dd3d4b68220d3c381f737eb2729d0017ed3271ce119d408b13\"\n  },\n  \"text\": {\n    \"encoding\": \"UTF-8, fatal decoding; BOM permitted and counts as content\",\n    \"separator\": \"LF; CRLF is one LF separator; isolated CR refuses\",\n    \"count\": \"Number of LF bytes plus one if nonempty content has no final LF\",\n    \"blankAndCommentLines\": \"included\",\n    \"otherUnicodeSeparators\": \"content, not LF\"\n  },\n  \"selection\": {\n    \"matcher\": \"existing wire/classes.matches; * stays within segment, ** whole segment crosses segments\",\n    \"empty\": \"Valid selector matching no file yields named unmeasured selector-no-match, never payable zero\",\n    \"fileIdentity\": \"named file of supplied snapshot; same bytes at two names remain two inputs\",\n    \"malformed\": \"empty/absolute/traversing paths, backslashes, controls and non-segment ** refuse\",\n    \"partialUnion\": \"Each selector has its own named selection status; a matched region union does not hide unmatched selectors or satisfy their demands\"\n  },\n  \"support\": {\n    \"atom\": \"named file, integer physical-line weight\",\n    \"composition\": \"Delegated to finiteRegionMeasure; overlap, disjointness and unassigned retained\",\n    \"noMatchRegions\": \"excluded from numeric valuation; remain explicitly unmeasured in region outputs\"\n  },\n  \"policy\": {\n    \"byteBudget\": \"Declared input-byte limit checked before digest/UTF8 scan\",\n    \"rowBudget\": \"Declared selector-code-units-times-candidates limit and delegated finiteRegionMeasure declared-input-rows limit; separate work sections\"\n  },\n  \"authentication\": \"Digest callback checks file bytes only; snapshot authority, completeness, selector origin and evidence coverage remain consuming-host obligations\",\n  \"consumer\": \"Bound compares ceilings, judges witness and widening, and produces BLOCK; Topos does not\",\n  \"quartet\": {\n    \"yes\": [\n      \"samples/physical-lines/yes/catalog.json\",\n      \"samples/physical-lines/yes/orchard.json\"\n    ],\n    \"no\": [\n      \"samples/physical-lines/no/catalog.json\",\n      \"samples/physical-lines/no/orchard.json\"\n    ],\n    \"unitVector\": \"test/physical-lines.test.ts\",\n    \"native\": \"Requires declared reader, consumer binding and native receipt; source tests alone do not close it\"\n  },\n  \"refusals\": [\n    \"physical-lines/profile\",\n    \"physical-lines/policy\",\n    \"physical-lines/file\",\n    \"physical-lines/duplicate-file\",\n    \"physical-lines/selector\",\n    \"physical-lines/duplicate-region\",\n    \"physical-lines/integrity\",\n    \"physical-lines/utf8\",\n    \"physical-lines/isolated-cr\",\n    \"physical-lines/digest-port\"\n  ],\n  \"unmeasured\": [\n    \"physical-lines/byte-budget\",\n    \"physical-lines/selection-budget\",\n    \"region-measure/budget\",\n    \"selector-no-match\"\n  ],\n  \"lifecycle\": \"This contract specifies interpretation, not admission or publication status. Consult selected standing, admission receipts and release approval.\"\n}\n" at=witness:contextual-reading-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/physical-lines-data shape=docs/contracts/physical-lines.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-portable-birth/1\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Describe a bounded public birth payload without transferring admission or local authority.\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Contract meaning is independent of a particular selection/admission/publication.\",\n  \"pure\": true,\n  \"reuse\": [\n    \"canonical wire\",\n    \"bounded record codec\",\n    \"recipient supplied occupied coordinates\"\n  ],\n  \"contract\": [\n    \"Origin digest plus canonical unsigned alphabet writes; byte and item budgets supplied by caller.\",\n    \"Only declared public-line fields are permitted; by/sig/epoch envelopes and authority/key/root/store/derived material are refused.\",\n    \"No filesystem, store, signer, root, historical admission or automatic installation is part of the profile.\",\n    \"Occupied coordinates produce named open pack/collision needs, never replacement.\",\n    \"Arbitrary data cannot be certified free of secrets by syntax: the public-data producer remains responsible for selection; the receiver never executes or lands these lines by inspection.\",\n    \"All original declaration bytes are preserved; incompatible declarations remain for the native consumer to judge.\"\n  ],\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Origin authentication\",\n    \"Consumer collision resolution and native coverage/admission\",\n    \"Public-data selection; no generic secret-detection claim\"\n  ],\n  \"quartet\": {\n    \"contract\": \"docs/contracts/portable-birth.json\",\n    \"positive\": \"samples/portable-birth/yes/*.json\",\n    \"vector\": \"vectors/native/portable-birth.cli.json\",\n    \"negative\": \"samples/portable-birth/no/*.json\"\n  },\n  \"readerBudgetMs\": 5000\n}\n" at=witness:portable-source-profile-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/portable-birth-data shape=docs/contracts/portable-birth.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-profile-composition/1\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Describe finite parent-by-digest profiles, declared field contracts and unambiguous category pins.\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Contract meaning is independent of a particular selection/admission/publication.\",\n  \"pure\": true,\n  \"reuse\": [\n    \"composePolicy\",\n    \"policyTransition\",\n    \"selected Obligations lattice through receiver PolicyField\",\n    \"reading-witness codec\",\n    \"bounded record codec\"\n  ],\n  \"contract\": [\n    \"Parent bytes are supplied by caller, checked by digest, decoded canonically and traversed under an explicit item/closure budget; no I/O or universal region list.\",\n    \"Missing parents remain needs/bytes; corrupted bytes refuse integrity; cycles refuse.\",\n    \"Each field names its semantic contract digest; receiver selects the PolicyField with matching coordinate. Uncatalogued semantics refuse.\",\n    \"Existing meet/order classifies narrowing or widening. Widening and non-meet replacement leave authorize-transition needs; adding a field is addition, never called narrowing.\",\n    \"A witness remains a reading declaration requiring verify-witness; attest never grants authority. A witness does not erase authorize-transition needs.\",\n    \"Category pins name category, class, algorithm and digest. Ambiguous inherited/own pins refuse instead of last-wins.\",\n    \"All ancestor constraints remain visible; inherited incompatible non-meet declarations are not silently overridden. No inverse of a reduced aggregate is reconstructed.\"\n  ],\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Witness signature/CI provenance and consuming policy acceptance\",\n    \"Authorization and native admission of widening or added permissions\",\n    \"Resolving incompatible inherited profiles or replacing category pins\"\n  ],\n  \"quartet\": {\n    \"contract\": \"docs/contracts/profile-composition.json\",\n    \"positive\": \"samples/profile-composition/yes/*.json\",\n    \"vector\": \"vectors/native/profile-composition.cli.json\",\n    \"negative\": \"samples/profile-composition/no/*.json\"\n  },\n  \"readerBudgetMs\": 5000\n}\n" at=witness:portable-source-profile-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/profile-composition-data shape=docs/contracts/profile-composition.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-projection-chain/1\",\n  \"consumes\": {\n    \"package\": \"@lapxo/obligations\",\n    \"version\": \"0.4.7\",\n    \"contract\": \"projection-chain-composition@1\",\n    \"contractDigest\": \"sha256:34add91f4dfd04d38490f85577fcbb95059a58803c8b82c4a82af2d265a421d9\",\n    \"function\": \"mixProjectionLoss\",\n    \"moduleDigest\": \"sha256:af9c6a3dbeda91981b394b61e187f916dc0e0304801b7b654ff3e025ebce94cb\"\n  },\n  \"inputs\": [\n    \"profile\",\n    \"atoms\",\n    \"f\",\n    \"g\",\n    \"direct?\",\n    \"prior?\",\n    \"policy\"\n  ],\n  \"domain\": \"Finite named atoms, total deterministic f:X->Y and g:Y->Z. Y is exactly the image of f. Optional direct:X->Z must equal g composed with f. One prior on X; Y prior is the exact pushforward returned by Obligations.\",\n  \"output\": {\n    \"unit\": \"bits\",\n    \"approximation\": \"binary64-log2\",\n    \"loss\": [\n      \"H(X|Y)\",\n      \"H(Y|Z)\",\n      \"H(X|Z)\"\n    ],\n    \"residual\": \"xz-xy-yz; reported, not silently rounded\",\n    \"certification\": \"Finite model evaluation; not a general Lean certificate\"\n  },\n  \"budget\": {\n    \"unit\": \"declared-configurations\",\n    \"required\": \"2*|X|+|Y|\",\n    \"exceeded\": \"unmeasured:mix-loss/work-budget\"\n  },\n  \"priorAbsent\": \"unmeasured:mix-loss/prior-required\",\n  \"refusals\": [\n    \"projection/profile\",\n    \"projection/domain\",\n    \"projection/policy\",\n    \"projection/non-chain\",\n    \"projection/randomized-map\",\n    \"projection/changed-prior\",\n    \"projection/evaluation\"\n  ],\n  \"unchanged\": [\n    \"M0 profile\",\n    \"wire protocol\",\n    \"algebra\",\n    \"existing ceilings\"\n  ],\n  \"pending\": [\n    \"consumer public delivery verification before a stable dependency pin\"\n  ],\n  \"retainedEvidence\": {\n    \"priorObligationsVersion\": \"0.4.6\",\n    \"localAdmissionEpochs\": [\n      22,\n      23\n    ],\n    \"nativeReadings\": 29,\n    \"nativeOpened\": 0,\n    \"scope\": \"Prior selected bytes and their receipts; not an admission of this updated metadata or dependency identity\"\n  },\n  \"alignment\": {\n    \"scope\": \"Focused consumed-surface comparison, not a universal algebra equivalence proof\",\n    \"compiledSurface\": \"164 unchanged files; measures index changed and region-measure added\",\n    \"focusedTestsPerVersion\": 28,\n    \"diagnosticSnapshotDigest\": \"sha256:67bee949bca5179c218952cccea925973644256d3a7b1a57a413ccf74b2839c5\",\n    \"mathematicalContractAndModule\": \"byte-identical between 0.4.6 and 0.4.7\",\n    \"receiptRule\": \"Complete transitive input identity still decides reuse; version labels or equal model outputs alone do not\"\n  },\n  \"lifecycle\": \"This contract specifies interpretation, not admission or publication status. Consult selected standing, admission receipts and release approval.\"\n}\n" at=witness:contextual-reading-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/projection-chain-data shape=docs/contracts/projection-chain.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-reading-witness/1\",\n  \"responsibility\": \"Pure representation and canonical bytes; existing host/consumer verifies provenance and applies policy\",\n  \"functions\": [\n    \"encodeReadingWitness\",\n    \"decodeReadingWitness\",\n    \"inspectReadingWitness\",\n    \"readingWitnessStatementBytes\"\n  ],\n  \"required\": [\n    \"class\",\n    \"reading\",\n    \"contract\",\n    \"model\",\n    \"params\",\n    \"inputs\",\n    \"selection\",\n    \"unit\",\n    \"scale\",\n    \"resolution\",\n    \"reader\",\n    \"implementation\",\n    \"context\",\n    \"run\",\n    \"result\",\n    \"authentication\",\n    \"evidence\"\n  ],\n  \"class\": \"attest\",\n  \"digests\": {\n    \"algorithm\": \"sha256\",\n    \"encoding\": \"sha256:<64 lowercase hex>\",\n    \"fields\": [\n      \"reading\",\n      \"contract\",\n      \"model\",\n      \"params\",\n      \"inputs\",\n      \"selection\",\n      \"scale\",\n      \"resolution\",\n      \"reader\",\n      \"implementation\",\n      \"context\",\n      \"result\",\n      \"evidence\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"authenticationProfiles\": {\n    \"key-covered\": {\n      \"required\": [\n        \"key\",\n        \"coverage\"\n      ],\n      \"meaning\": \"Declared key/coverage evidence; signature and admission not verified\"\n    },\n    \"ci-run-unkeyed\": {\n      \"required\": [\n        \"repository\",\n        \"commit\",\n        \"workflow\",\n        \"attempt\"\n      ],\n      \"meaning\": \"Declared CI-run provenance; no place-key signature implied\",\n      \"attempt\": \"positive canonical decimal\",\n      \"workflow\": \"sha256 digest\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"canonical\": \"Existing bound-lock/1 field codec, separate top-level profile, roundtrip exact bytes; no extra fields\",\n  \"identity\": \"Canonical complete witness bytes; host computes digest\",\n  \"statement\": {\n    \"profile\": \"topos-reading-statement/1\",\n    \"fields\": \"all canonical witness fields except evidence\",\n    \"reason\": \"covering proof cannot include its own digest\"\n  },\n  \"result\": {\n    \"status\": \"declared\",\n    \"authentication\": \"not verified\",\n    \"authorization\": \"not established\"\n  },\n  \"needsVerification\": [\n    \"referenced bytes and full reading/context/result bindings\",\n    \"model parameters, unit, scale composition law and resolution\",\n    \"key coverage/signature or CI run/attempt provenance under declared trust path\",\n    \"consuming operation policy acceptance\"\n  ],\n  \"refusals\": [\n    \"reading-witness/record\",\n    \"reading-witness/authentication-profile\",\n    \"reading-witness/fields\",\n    \"reading-witness/field-value\",\n    \"reading-witness/reading-class\",\n    \"reading-witness/digest\",\n    \"reading-witness/coverage\",\n    \"reading-witness/ci-context\",\n    \"reading-witness/profile\",\n    \"reading-witness/canonical-bytes\"\n  ],\n  \"vectors\": {\n    \"positive\": [\n      \"samples/reading-witness/yes/catalog.json\",\n      \"samples/reading-witness/yes/orchard.json\"\n    ],\n    \"negative\": [\n      \"samples/reading-witness/no/catalog.json\",\n      \"samples/reading-witness/no/orchard.json\"\n    ],\n    \"test\": \"test/reading-witness.test.ts\",\n    \"scope\": \"Pure schema/canonicality and identity preimages; sample digests are synthetic, not verified evidence\"\n  },\n  \"pending\": [\n    \"native consumer verification of actual provenance and policy acceptance\"\n  ],\n  \"excluded\": [\n    \"authority decisions\",\n    \"signature implementation\",\n    \"network/host IO\",\n    \"ambient clock\",\n    \"universal distributivity\",\n    \"independence inferred from labels\"\n  ],\n  \"lifecycle\": \"This contract specifies interpretation, not admission or publication status. Consult selected standing, admission receipts and release approval.\"\n}\n" at=witness:contextual-reading-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/reading-witness-data shape=docs/contracts/reading-witness.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-reference-projection/1\",\n  \"purpose\": \"A separate bounded inline preview and declared relation profile; historical references retain their exact meaning.\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Meaning is independent of a particular owner selection or release.\",\n  \"contract\": [\n    \"#bound:1 and #topos-reference:1 bytes/constructors remain unchanged. The new wrapper never inserts syntax into either historical profile.\",\n    \"Receiver declares inline UTF-8 byte limit; overflow refuses, never truncates. Inline text has an exact digest.\",\n    \"Duplicate relations require explicit preserve/refuse. Relation names and target digests are declarations, not truth.\",\n    \"Preview bytes never replace complete standing bytes or authenticate their origin. Full content remains needs/bytes/<blob>.\",\n    \"A fragment is readable by page code; secrecy is not promised. Producers must not include secrets inline.\",\n    \"Holder and viewer remain distinct locator classes; a viewer URL is not assumed to be a raw-byte endpoint. Availability, byte integrity and admitted disagreement remain different.\",\n    \"The existing contextual meaning of none is retained; there is no silent new literal rule.\"\n  ],\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Projection interpretation/completeness, relation verification and authenticity\",\n    \"Transport/origin policy and actual content resolution\"\n  ],\n  \"quartet\": {\n    \"contract\": \"docs/contracts/reference-compatibility.json\",\n    \"positive\": \"samples/reference-compatibility/yes/*.json\",\n    \"vector\": \"vectors/native/reference-compatibility.cli.json\",\n    \"negative\": \"samples/reference-compatibility/no/*.json\"\n  },\n  \"readerBudgetMs\": 5000\n}\n" at=witness:reference-wire-catalog-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/reference-compatibility-data shape=docs/contracts/reference-compatibility.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-refusal-catalog/1\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Machine-readable exact producer/code catalog for the declared new-form surface, with observed producer vectors and separately open external demands.\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Meaning is independent of a particular owner selection or release.\",\n  \"contract\": [\n    \"vectors/refusal-catalog.json is the data source. This Markdown table is derived; no consumer parses prose.\",\n    \"Every local entry names producer, implementation digest, exact code, class, meaning, next, vector and case. All65 local causes were observed in two unrelated contexts.\",\n    \"Next names resolve to catalog actions; duplicate producer/code pairs, unresolved next and malformed definitions refuse. No executable action or authority is carried by next.\",\n    \"Catalog identity preimage is encodeRefusalCatalog(data,budget) followed by one LF. Authority/action context commits this identity alongside standingContract; the receiver selects both.\",\n    \"Lookup returns declared metadata, never producer authenticity or authority. Unknown/external producer codes remain named open needs.\",\n    \"This scope covers the declared0.2.4 new forms. Legacy wire/reference cause bytes remain in compatibility fixtures, without inventing slash aliases.\",\n    \"Five Head door codes, github-runs-on and doc-install-region remain seven named producer demands until their actual contract/version/vector arrives.\",\n    \"The older governance-refusals draft is historical evidence; it is not the newly selected catalog.\"\n  ],\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Producer authentication, consumer acceptance and next-action execution\",\n    \"The seven external producer demands\"\n  ],\n  \"quartet\": {\n    \"contract\": \"docs/contracts/refusal-catalog.json\",\n    \"positive\": \"samples/refusal-catalog/yes/*.json\",\n    \"vector\": \"vectors/native/refusal-catalog.cli.json\",\n    \"negative\": \"samples/refusal-catalog/no/*.json\"\n  },\n  \"readerBudgetMs\": 5000\n}\n" at=witness:reference-wire-catalog-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/refusal-catalog-data shape=docs/contracts/refusal-catalog.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"id\": \"topos-source-exhaustion/1\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Represent source exhaustion, attributed events and known/unknown recovery without implementing budgets or scheduling.\",\n  \"lifecycle\": \"Contract meaning is independent of a particular selection/admission/publication.\",\n  \"pure\": true,\n  \"reuse\": [\n    \"source-card canonical bytes and digest\",\n    \"registry explicit clock/unit horizon\",\n    \"bounded record codec\"\n  ],\n  \"contract\": [\n    \"Binds the exact source card, source, cost unit, observation evidence, explicit exhaustedAt and knownSince in a declared frame.\",\n    \"Events have distinct IDs and evidence digests; duplication refuses rather than charging twice.\",\n    \"Declared recovery names its time and evidence; unknown recovery has neither invented time nor evidence.\",\n    \"Recovery cannot precede exhaustion; consumer-selected source, clock and time unit must match.\",\n    \"Cost unit and time unit are distinct. No Date.now, network, mutable counters or retry scheduler.\",\n    \"Source-card decoding names the declaration; source-card form conformance, observation authentication, actual budget exhaustion and acceptance remain consumer obligations.\"\n  ],\n  \"externalObligations\": [\n    \"Signature or provenance of events and exhaustion\",\n    \"Source-card catalog/form conformance\",\n    \"Ceiling comparison, eligibility to retry and credit resets\"\n  ],\n  \"quartet\": {\n    \"contract\": \"docs/contracts/source-exhaustion.json\",\n    \"positive\": \"samples/source-exhaustion/yes/*.json\",\n    \"vector\": \"vectors/native/source-exhaustion.cli.json\",\n    \"negative\": \"samples/source-exhaustion/no/*.json\"\n  },\n  \"readerBudgetMs\": 5000\n}\n" at=witness:portable-source-profile-contracts by=target form=alphabet measure=text role=writes scope=prose/en/contracts/source-exhaustion-data shape=docs/contracts/source-exhaustion.json value=lock
bound-lock/1 about="{\n  \"name\": \"@lapxo/topos\",\n  \"version\": \"0.2.4\",\n  \"description\": \"Wire, forms, authority and views for interpreting information.\",\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"license\": \"MIT\",\n  \"author\": \"Lapxo\",\n  \"repository\": {\n    \"type\": \"git\",\n    \"url\": \"git+https://github.com/Lapxo/topos.git\"\n  },\n  \"keywords\": [\n    \"topos\",\n    \"lock\",\n    \"wire\",\n    \"capsule\"\n  ],\n  \"sideEffects\": false,\n  \"engines\": {\n    \"node\": \">=22.12\"\n  },\n  \"exports\": {\n    \".\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/readers/index.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/readers/index.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/readers/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./authority\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/authority/index.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/authority/index.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/authority/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./capsule\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/capsule/index.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/capsule/index.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/capsule/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./contract\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/contract/index.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/contract/index.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/contract/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./forms\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/forms/index.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/forms/index.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/forms/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./host\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/host/index.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/host/index.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/host/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./readers\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/readers/index.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/readers/index.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/readers/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./wire\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/wire/index.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/wire/index.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/wire/index.js\"\n    },\n    \"./package.json\": \"./package.json\",\n    \"./object-provider\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/host/object-provider.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/host/object-provider.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/host/object-provider.js\"\n    },\n    \"./standing\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/topos/standing.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/topos/standing.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/topos/standing.js\"\n    },\n    \"./cells-view\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/views/cells.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/views/cells.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/views/cells.js\"\n    },\n    \"./cell-inputs\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/views/cell-inputs.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/views/cell-inputs.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/views/cell-inputs.js\"\n    },\n    \"./vectors/evidence.json\": \"./vectors/evidence.json\",\n    \"./receipts\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/receipts.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/receipts.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/receipts.js\"\n    },\n    \"./vectors/signing-port.json\": \"./vectors/signing-port.json\",\n    \"./walk\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/walk.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/walk.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/walk.js\"\n    },\n    \"./core\": {\n      \"types\": \"./dist/core.d.ts\",\n      \"source\": \"./src/core.ts\",\n      \"default\": \"./dist/core.js\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"files\": [\n    \"dist\",\n    \"README.md\",\n    \"CONTRIBUTING.md\",\n    \"CITATION.cff\",\n    \"LICENSE\",\n    \"TARGET.bound\",\n    \"receipts.bound\",\n    \"docs\",\n    \"vectors/evidence.json\",\n    \"vectors/signing-port.json\",\n    \"samples/walk/*.json\",\n    \"vectors/walk.json\",\n    \"src/**/*.ts\",\n    \"samples/programs/*.json\",\n    \"samples/public-boundary/*.json\",\n    \"vectors/public-boundary.json\",\n    \"samples/readings/*.json\",\n    \"vectors/readings.json\",\n    \"samples/yes/two-origins-meet-on-one-scope.json\",\n    \"samples/yes/three-origins-two-meet-one-apart.json\",\n    \"samples/yes/render-world.json\",\n    \"vectors/canonical-compatibility.json\",\n    \"vectors/order.cli.json\",\n    \"vectors/native/*.cli.json\",\n    \"vectors/wire/fields.json\",\n    \"vectors/forms.json\",\n    \"vectors/reading-identity.json\",\n    \"samples/place-inputs/*.json\",\n    \"vectors/native/place-inputs.cli.json\",\n    \"samples/place-act-context/*.json\",\n    \"vectors/place-act-context/*.json\",\n    \"samples/authority-eligibility/*.json\",\n    \"vectors/native/authority-eligibility.cli.json\",\n    \"vectors/native/object-effective-order.cli.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/temperature-band/TARGET.bound\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/temperature-band/inputs/sample.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/temperature-band/package.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/temperature-band/reader.js\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/temperature-band/receipts.bound\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/editorial-stage/TARGET.bound\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/editorial-stage/inputs/sample.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/editorial-stage/package.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/editorial-stage/reader.js\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/yes/editorial-stage/receipts.bound\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/temperature-band/TARGET.bound\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/temperature-band/inputs/sample.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/temperature-band/package.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/temperature-band/reader.js\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/temperature-band/receipts.bound\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/editorial-stage/TARGET.bound\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/editorial-stage/inputs/sample.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/editorial-stage/package.json\",\n    \"samples/object-effective-order/no/editorial-stag